{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Happy is the man</b> — Our predecessors of blessed memory said: that עמד is harsher than הלך, and ישב is harshest of all. If so, the לצים are worse than sinners. And R. Moses the Cohen explained: the reverse, and said: that the sense of לא עמד is 'did not even stand.' And in my opinion: the word רשעים refers to those who do not stand on a fixed course, as in the manner of ורשעים כים נגרש (and the wicked are like the tossing sea), כי השקט לא יוכל (for it cannot be still), and likewise ובכל אשר יפנה ירשיע (and wherever he turns he acts wickedly) and הוא ישקיט ומי ירשיע (he quiets — and who can act wickedly?). And on account of this he mentioned with רשעים the הלך, which is the one who is persuaded to walk after the counsel of another wicked person, ובדרך לא ידעה (and in a way he did not know)." "<b>And the word חטאים</b> — is difficult, and on account of this he mentioned דרך, which is the path he is accustomed to walk in." "<b>And the word ישב</b> — is harsher than it, and so is the opinion of the predecessors." "<b>לצים</b> — from the root of מליץ, as in כי המליץ בינותם (for the interpreter was between them), which is, he reveals the secret of Reuben to Simeon. And the לצים are the opposite of the humble, as it says: אם ללצים הוא יליץ (to scorners he is scornful) and after it ולענוים יתן חן (but to the humble he gives grace), and the humble are the bashful — to speak slander and to cast aspersion and to reveal secrets. And in the Shema there are four postures of the body, namely: בשבתך (when you sit), and the opposite: בלכתך (when you walk), for motion is the opposite of rest, and בשכבך (when you lie down) the opposite of: ובקומך (when you rise). And in the Psalms, ישב corresponds to בשבתך, and likewise הלך corresponds to לכתך, and likewise עמד corresponds to קם; and he did not mention lying down, because most people sleep. And the rule of the holy tongue is to insert a sign-letter for all verbs when they are in the future: from פעל to יפעל; and when they wish to speak of standing time, they speak in past tense — also in the future, as in וינועו אמות הספים והבית ימלא עשן (and the thresholds will shake and the house will fill with smoke). And so: לא הלך — and in his Torah he meditates, for he has no business or desire in the vanities of the world; rather, all his desire is in the Torah of HaShem, to perform the commandments." "<b>And the sense of תורה</b> — that our Torah is the straight path." "<b>And the word יהגה</b> — in the heart, and like it: והגות לבי תבונות (and the meditation of my heart — understandings); also in the mouth, as in: ולשוני תהגה צדקך (and my tongue will utter your righteousness). And as for saying ובתורתו יהגה and it was not written ובה יהגה — it is a matter of eloquence, for the word ישראל appears five times in a single verse." "<b>And he mentioned יומם ולילה (day and night)</b> — corresponding to the four postures of the body." "<b>And the word יהגה</b> — in the heart, and like it: והגות לבי תבונות (and the meditation of my heart — understandings); also in the mouth, as in: ולשוני תהגה צדקך (and my tongue will utter your righteousness)." "<b>And as for saying ובתורתו יהגה and it was not written ובה יהגה</b> — it is a matter of eloquence, for the word ישראל appears five times in a single verse." "<b>And he mentioned יומם ולילה (day and night)</b> — corresponding to the four postures of the body."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:13.607536314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}